# Never upload local env files to the Vercel build — runtime uses the
# dashboard environment variables. (Runtime is already secure; this keeps
# secrets out of the build container entirely.)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local-only / not needed for the build
.git
tests
playwright-report
test-results
*.log
scratchpad

# Native shells. The Vercel build produces the WEB app only; the Capacitor
# projects and the mobile SPA are built separately. Excluded so nothing here can
# affect (or slow) a production web deploy.
#
# THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. .vercelignore follows .gitignore matching,
# where an unrooted pattern matches a directory of that name at ANY depth. Bare
# `mobile` therefore also excluded `src/lib/mobile/` and — critically —
# `src/app/api/mobile/`, the mobile RPC route. The result was a production
# backend that had never once served /api/mobile/**, so the first APK installed
# on a real phone died on launch: the CORS preflight hit a 404 page carrying no
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin, and the WebView blocked the request.
#
# Nothing in the build reported it. The route simply was not in the upload.
# src/app/api/mobile/deployment.test.ts now fails if an unrooted pattern can reach src/.
/ios
/mobile
/android
